why: the operator's objection, and it is right: the section explains
  Facts with `Fact[String]` and `Fact[Int]`, which show the machinery
  and motivate nothing. It never says WHY a fact exists rather than a
  capability — installation SHADOWS, contribution ACCUMULATES — and
  the worked examples are toys.

what: rewrite the section around the three cases this repository
  actually has: routes contributed by feature modules and served
  merged (PartialFunction is a monoid under orElse), health checks a
  reader collects, and the deployment needs already shipped. The
  routes example COMPILES, in okay-http's tests, with the real
  Request/Response types.

next: write the compiled routes example, then rewrite the section
